+# FACKTS Hoops authentication and email setup
+
+This release keeps the two account types separate:
+
+- Admins are Supabase Auth users approved in `admin_profiles`.
+- Players are Supabase Auth users linked to one active official row in `players.user_id`.
+- Guest hoopers and prospects are not eligible for player portal access.
+
+## 1. Run the Supabase migration
+
+Open the Supabase SQL Editor for the FACKTS project and run:
+
+`supabase/migrations/20260721_player_auth.sql`
+
+This adds the player-to-auth link and the focused access policies used by the login flow.
+
+## 2. Add Vercel environment variables
+
+Add these variables to Production, Preview, and Development where appropriate:
+
+- `NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL`
+- `NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY`
+- `SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY`
+- `NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL=https://fackts-hoops-web.vercel.app`
+- `RESEND_API_KEY`
+- `EMAIL_FROM=FACKTS Hoops <notifications@your-verified-domain.com>`
+- `FACKTS_ADMIN_EMAIL=facktsafrica@gmail.com`
+
+Important:
+
+- Never prefix the service-role key or Resend key with `NEXT_PUBLIC_`.
+- `EMAIL_FROM` must use the exact domain that Resend approved.
+- Use a Resend API key restricted to sending if possible.
+- Redeploy after changing Vercel environment variables.
+
+In Supabase **Authentication → URL Configuration**, add the live site URL and allow this redirect path:
+
+`https://fackts-hoops-web.vercel.app/account/update-password`
+
+For local testing, also allow:
+
+`http://localhost:3000/account/update-password`
+
+## 3. Verify admin access
+
+1. Open `/admin/login`.
+2. Log in using an existing Supabase Auth administrator.
+3. The user must have an active row in `admin_profiles`.
+4. Open **Email Notifications** and send a test email.
+
+## 4. Issue player accounts
+
+1. Open `/admin/player-access`.
+2. Choose an active official player.
+3. Confirm the player email.
+4. Select **Invite Player**.
+5. Resend delivers a branded secure activation link.
+6. The player sets a password and enters `/player`.
+
+Use **Resend Access** when the player needs a fresh secure link. **Revoke Access** removes the player-to-account link without deleting the public player profile.
+
+## 5. Notification rules
+
+- A player availability response emails `FACKTS_ADMIN_EMAIL`.
+- A player 1v1 challenge request emails `FACKTS_ADMIN_EMAIL`.
+- Admin approval emails the available player recipients.
+- The email API requires an approved FACKTS login and no longer acts as a public email relay.
